2026-10-15 17:59 UTC — closed one P18-V01 Remoting codec behavior mismatch.

Pinned Java 5.5.1 `RocketMQSerializable` uses `writeShort` for both request
code and version, so i32 inputs retain their low 16 bits. The Rust private
header encoder previously rejected values outside the signed range. Added a
Java-generated `PRIVATE-LARGE-CODE-VERSION` frame for code/version `987654`,
which decode as `4614`; the new Rust regression first failed with
`FieldTooWide("code")`. Rust now narrows both fields exactly like Java, and
the complete encoded frame matches byte-for-byte. Removed this resolved item
from `KNOWN_DIFFERENCES.md` and added the new fixture to the compatibility
matrix.

Validation passed: `cargo test -p rocketmq-classic-remoting --all-features
--locked` (96 unit, 7 codec, 1 fuzz regression, 5 security, 100 transport and
5 doctests); strict all-target/all-feature Remoting Clippy; Maven verify (37
scenarios); `cargo fmt --all -- --check`; `git diff --check`; and byte-for-byte
comparison of the checked-in fixture against fresh pinned-Java output. Fixture
SHA-256: `033e89778d92def6f5e1875211ea4ca7b59facaf813a72a57de8c386c5e4acf8`.
Code/test/fixture/compatibility-matrix commit: `c0878056`. Broad P18-V01,
current GitHub Ubuntu/P18-V04 evidence, Phase 19 local Docker/Broker automation
and release version/registry resolution remain open. No plan, push, tag,
publication, deployment or live Broker action occurred.

2026-10-15 18:09 UTC — closed a second P18-V01 Remoting serialization mismatch.

Pinned Java 5.5.1 `RocketMQSerializable.writeStr(true, key)` writes the UTF-8
key byte count with `setShort`, retaining only its low 16 bits while keeping
the full key bytes. Added an oracle frame with a 32,768-byte key; its wire
length is `0x8000` (signed `-32768`). The Rust regression first failed with
`FieldTooWide("ext field key")`; the encoder now matches Java byte-for-byte.
The fixture is in `fixtures/remoting/edge-cases/` because the intentionally
wrapped length makes it invalid for ordinary decoding.

Validation passed: `cargo test -p rocketmq-classic-remoting --all-features
--locked` (96 unit, 8 codec, 1 fuzz regression, 5 security, 100 transport and
5 doctests); strict all-target/all-feature Remoting Clippy; Maven verify (37
scenarios); rustfmt, diff checks and fixture comparison against freshly
generated Java output. Fixture SHA-256:
`7af64d29f396b2e7a1dd70a57066920890559fce1f170844ca8d4e1ba3a453ca`. Commit
`c62e0740` closes this private-key-length slice only. Broad P18-V01, current
